---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { iems, meta, removed } from '../lib/data';
import { PDF_URL, LINKEDIN_URL, AUTHOR } from '../lib/site';

const tally = new Map<string, number>();
for (const i of iems) for (const m of i.measurers) tally.set(m, (tally.get(m) ?? 0) + 1);
const measurers = [...tally.entries()].sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1] || a[0].localeCompare(b[0]));
---

<Base
  title="About and credits · IEM India"
  description="Who made IEM India, whose measurements it stands on, and what the data cannot tell you."
>
  <article class="narrow page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Credits, sources and limits.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm {AUTHOR}. I built this over a Diwali break because choosing a first IEM in India is confusing, and I wanted
      to see what the measurements say once the marketing is taken away.
    </p>
    <p class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href={PDF_URL}>Read the write-up (PDF)</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href={LINKEDIN_URL}>LinkedIn</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/how">How I did it</a>
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>The people who measured</h2>
      <p>
        Every sound score here rests on someone else's careful work. {measurers.length} independent measurers publish
        their frequency responses on squig.link. Thank you to each of them. The number is how many IEMs on this site
        use their data.
      </p>
      <ul class="measurers">
        {
          measurers.map(([m, n]) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`https://${m}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                {m}
              </a>
              <span>{n}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p>
        The measurements were compiled by the open-source
        <a href="https://github.com/PEQHUB/Squig-Rank" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Squig-Rank</a> project,
        which made this possible.
      </p>
      <p class="note">{meta.disclaimers[3]}</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>Each source is labelled as evidence (papers and documents) or data.</p>
      <ul class="sources">
        {
          meta.sources.map((s) => (
            <li class="card">
              <span class={`badge ${s.type.startsWith('evidence') ? 'ok' : ''}`}>{s.type}</span>
              <b>{s.name}</b>
              <span class="muted">Used for: {s.used_for}.</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="small muted">
        The Harman in-ear model is from Olive, Welti and Khonsaripour, presented at the Audio Engineering Society in
        2017 (AES papers 9840 and 9878).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What I chose not to collect</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        {meta.exclusions.map((e) => <li>{e}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        {meta.disclaimers.map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}
        <li>
          {removed.length} IEMs were removed as discontinued. <a href="/how#removed">They are listed, with reasons</a>.
        </li>
        <li>Prices and stock were read on {meta.built}. They will have changed. Check the store before you buy.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No strings</h2>
      <p>
        This is not a shop. There are no affiliate links, no sponsors and no tracking beyond basic page analytics from
        the host. The store links go straight to the product page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Product photos belong to the stores. They are loaded from the store that lists the product, not copied here,
        and each one is credited beside the photo.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 3.4rem);
  }
  section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .measurers {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    columns: 2;
    column-gap: 1.2rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  .measurers li {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .measurers a {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    padding: 0.15rem 0;
  }
  .measurers span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sources {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .sources li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
    justify-items: start;
  }
  .list {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .measurers {
      columns: 3;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }
  }
</style>
